namespace: biological_process
def: "The aggregation, arrangement and bonding together of a set of components to form a ruffle, a projection at the leading edge of a crawling cell; the protrusions are supported by a microfilament meshwork. The formation of ruffles (also called membrane ruffling) is thought to be controlled by a group of enzymes known as Rho GTPases, specifically RhoA, Rac1 and cdc42." [GOC:yaf, http:en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Membrane_ruffling, PMID:12556481]
