def: "Binding to a toxin to prevent it from interacting with other partners or to inhibit its localization to the area of the cell or complex where it is active." [GOC:rs, PMID:19143615, PMID:19325885, PMID:21819231, PMID:22545240, PMID:24806488, Wikipedia:Toxin-antitoxin_system#Type_II]
comment: There may be more than one antitoxin to a toxic protein. Instances of this activity are known only in prokaryotes, where the toxic protein may be a ribonuclease, a DNA gyrase, or other.
