def: "OBSOLETE. A process carried out at the cellular level, which is the final step in vesicle assembly. Vesicle fusion occurs when a newly assembled vesicle closes up, following vesicle vesicle scission (GO:0099050)." [GOC:aruk, GOC:bc, PMID:25898166]
comment: This term was made obsolete becausethat 'fusion' should only be used for two membranes getting joined together, whereas in this case it would be one membrane 'closing/sealing up'.
