[Term]
id: GO:0140621
name: type I pilus
namespace: cellular_component
def: "A short filamentous structure on the surface of a bacterial cell distinguished from other pili by their D-mannose-sensitive agglutinatination of erythrocytes. In E. coli, type I pili consist of a short tip fibrillum made up of the adhesin protein (FimH) and two minor subunits (FimG and FimF) that is joined to the pilus rod, a homopolymer of ~1000 FimA subunits." [PMID:28496159, PMID:29345620]
synonym: "type 1 pilus" EXACT []
synonym: "type I fimbriae" EXACT []
synonym: "type I pili" EXACT []
