[Term]
id: GO:1900447
name: regulation of cell morphogenesis involved in phenotypic switching
namespace: biological_process
def: "Any process that modulates the frequency, rate or extent of cell morphogenesis contributing a phenotypic switch. Cell morphogenesis involved in differentiation is the change in form (cell shape and size) that occurs when relatively unspecialized cells, such as the opaque cells of C. albicans, acquire specialized structural and/or functional features that characterize the cells, tissues, or organs of the mature organism or some other relatively stable phase of the organism's life history." [GOC:di, GOC:TermGenie]
synonym: "negative regulation of cell shape and cell size of phenotypic dimorphism" RELATED [GOC:TermGenie]
