[Term]
id: GO:1901680
name: sulfur-containing amino acid secondary active transmembrane transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Enables the transfer of sulfur-containing amino acid from one side of a membrane to the other, up its concentration gradient. The transporter binds the solute and undergoes a series of conformational changes. Transport works equally well in either direction and is driven by a chemiosmotic source of energy. Secondary active transporters include symporters and antiporters." [GOC:pr, GOC:TermGenie]
