[Term]
id: GO:1903289
name: obsolete regulation of ATP catabolic process
namespace: biological_process
def: "OBSOLETE. Any process that modulates the frequency, rate or extent of ATP catabolic process." [GO_REF:0000058, GOC:BHF, GOC:rl, GOC:TermGenie, PMID:10636900]
comment: The reason for making this term obsolete is that it gets misused in cases where phosphates are simply being removed from a small molecule. We found no cases where these molecules genuinely underwent catabolism.
