[Term]
id: GO:1905906
name: regulation of amyloid fibril formation
namespace: biological_process
def: "Any process that modulates the frequency, rate or extent of amyloid fibril formation." [GO_REF:0000058, GOC:aruk, GOC:bc, GOC:TermGenie, PMID:23106396]
comment: Although deposition of amyloid fibrils is associated with diseases, e.g. Alzheimer's disease, amyloid formation is a normal process. Disease occurs when the balance between amyloid formation and clearance is disrupted (reviewed e.g. in PMID:29654159 and PMID:28937655). An example of a normal amyloid complex is composed of human RIP1 and RIP3 kinases (PMID:22817896).
synonym: "regulation of amyloid fibril assembly" RELATED [GOC:TermGenie]
synonym: "regulation of amyloid structure assembly" RELATED [GOC:TermGenie]
synonym: "regulation of amyloid structure formation" RELATED [GOC:TermGenie]
