[Term]
id: GO:1990205
name: taurine dioxygenase complex
namespace: cellular_component
def: "A protein complex capable of catalyzing the conversion of taurine and alpha-ketoglutarate to sulfite, aminoacetaldehyde and succinate under sulfur or cysteine starvation conditions. Its expression is repressed by the presence of sulfate or cysteine. In E. coli it is a homodimer or homotetramer of the protein TauD." [GOC:bhm, PMID:12741810]
synonym: "2-aminoethanesulfonate dioxygenase complex" EXACT []
synonym: "alpha-ketoglutarate-dependent taurine dioxygenase complex" EXACT []
