namespace: biological_process
def: "OBSOLETE. The chemical reactions and pathways resulting in the formation of a monounsaturated fatty acid. A monounsaturated fatty acid has one double bond in the fatty acid chain with all of the remainder carbon atoms being single-bonded, as opposed to polyunsaturated fatty acids." [GOC:hjd, PMID:16443825]
comment: For example, stearoyl-coenzyme A desaturase (Scd) catalyzes the desaturation of saturated fatty acids to monounsaturated fatty acids in mammals and yeast.
